                "type": "text",
                "text": "Add the water fractions and oil fractions separately for the equal bottle volumes.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let each bottle contain $V$ litres.\n\nBottle 1 contains $\\frac{3V}{5}$ litres of water and $\\frac{2V}{5}$ litres of oil. Bottle 2 contains $\\frac{5V}{11}$ litres of water and $\\frac{6V}{11}$ litres of oil.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Combined water}&=\\frac{3V}{5}+\\frac{5V}{11}\\\\\\text{Combined water}&=\\frac{33V+25V}{55}\\\\\\text{Combined water}&=\\frac{58V}{55}\\text{ litres}\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Combined oil}&=\\frac{2V}{5}+\\frac{6V}{11}\\\\\\text{Combined oil}&=\\frac{22V+30V}{55}\\\\\\text{Combined oil}&=\\frac{52V}{55}\\text{ litres}\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Water}:\\text{oil}&=\\frac{58V}{55}:\\frac{52V}{55}\\\\\\text{Water}:\\text{oil}&=58:52\\\\\\text{Water}:\\text{oil}&=29:26\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
